    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d984">

                <pb facs="1231" n="1213" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg1213"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.85/4–1046: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Pawley</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">u.s. urgent</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-04-10T19:00:00-05:00">April 10, 1946—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>331. Approval has been given by Dept to sale from surplus of following vessels to
                    Peru (your 372 Apr 1<anchor n="15" xml:id="d984-f1"/>). You may inform Peruvian
                    authorities. Navy Dept has informally discussed matter with Peruvian
                    representatives.</p>
                <list>
                    <item>6 Submarine chasers (SC)</item>
                    <item>8 Landing Craft, Infantry, (Gunboat) (LCI(G))</item>
                    <item>2 Oilers (AO)</item>
                    <item>2 Rescue Tugs (ATR)</item>
                    <item>10 Landing Vehicles, tracked (LVT)</item>
                    <item>1 Gunboat (PG)</item>
                    <item>3 Landing Craft, tank (LCT)</item>
                </list>
                <p>Symbols in parentheses refer to Navy nomenclature for vessels concerned.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
